  {
   "author": {
    "login": "Ian-cmd-ops"
   },
   "authorAssociation": "NONE",
   "body": "@bherbruck Thanks. The description is filled in now. The saved seed is a case the test got wrong, not the kernel. Those two boxes touch only along an edge line, so union is refused on purpose (\u201czero-thickness edge contact\u201d). Intersect (empty) and cut (562.5 mm\u00b3) match the closed form. The first version of box_box_exact expected a union volume there. It now accepts an error for edge-only contact, but never a wrong volume, and the seed passes. I kept the seed committed so every run checks that case first. The defaults took 159 s (boolean_props) and 802 s (atomic_commands) on 2 cores, measured on 0872eb95. Most of atomic_commands is fuzz seed 0.",
